{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Gigantic is an American comedy-drama television series that aired on TeenNick.","title":"Gigantic (TV series)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The series ran from on October 8, 2010 to April 22, 2010.","title":"Gigantic (TV series)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Ryan Rottman (born March 17, 1984) is an American actor.","title":"Ryan Rottman"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is known for his role as Joey Colvin on the TeenNick series "Gigantic".","title":"Ryan Rottman"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The 2010 Northern Hemisphere summer heat waves included severe heat waves that impacted most of the United States, Kazakhstan, Mongolia, China, Hong Kong, North Africa and the European continent as a whole, along with parts of Canada, Russia, Indochina, South Korea and Japan during May, June, July, and August 2010.","title":"2010 Northern Hemisphere summer heat waves"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The first phase of the global heatwaves was caused by a moderate El Niño event, which lasted from June 2009 to May 2010.","title":"2010 Northern Hemisphere summer heat waves"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The first phase lasted only from April 2010 to June 2010, and caused only moderate above average temperatures in the areas affected.","title":"2010 Northern Hemisphere summer heat waves"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" But it also set new record high temperatures for most of the area affected, in the Northern Hemisphere.","title":"2010 Northern Hemisphere summer heat waves"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The second phase (the main, and most devastating phase) was caused by a very strong La Niña event, which lasted from June 2010 to June 2011.","title":"2010 Northern Hemisphere summer heat waves"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" According to meteorologists, the 2010–11 La Niña event was one of the strongest La Niña events ever observed.","title":"2010 Northern Hemisphere summer heat waves"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" That same La Niña event also had devastating effects in the Eastern states of Australia.","title":"2010 Northern Hemisphere summer heat waves"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" The second phase lasted from June 2010 to October 2010, caused severe heat waves, and multiple record-breaking temperatures.","title":"2010 Northern Hemisphere summer heat waves"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" The heatwaves began on April 2010, when strong anticyclones began to develop, over most of the affected regions, in the Northern Hemisphere.","title":"2010 Northern Hemisphere summer heat waves"},{"sentence_id":9,"text":" The heatwaves ended in October 2010, when the powerful anticyclones over most of the affected areas dissipated.","title":"2010 Northern Hemisphere summer heat waves"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Joey's Song is the name of a series of music compilation CDs featuring nationally and internationally known artists who are donating their music to help raise awareness and monies to fight epilepsy.","title":"Joey's Song (CD series)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The "Joey's Song" CD series was launched by The Joseph Gomoll Foundation.","title":"Joey's Song (CD series)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The Joseph Gomoll Foundation was started in April 2010 following the death of 4-year-old Joey Gomoll.","title":"Joey's Song (CD series)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Over 100 artists have agreed to support and contribute original and rare musical content to the "Joey's Song" series of CDs.","title":"Joey's Song (CD series)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Wasted In Jackson is the debut studio album recorded by American singer-songwriter Lauren Pritchard, produced by Eg White and was released on 25 October 2010 on Island Records.","title":"Wasted in Jackson"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The album was digitally released on 25 October 2010, followed by a physical release on 25 October 2010 through Island Records.","title":"Wasted in Jackson"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The lead single from the album, "When the Night Kills the Day", was released on 3 May 2010.","title":"Wasted in Jackson"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" A second single from the album, "Painkillers", was released on 9 August 2010.","title":"Wasted in Jackson"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" A third single from the album, "Not the Drinking", was released on 25 October 2010, the same day as the album's release.","title":"Wasted in Jackson"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" "Not The Drinking" was the only single not to be released physically.","title":"Wasted in Jackson"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" All singles have so far failed to chart.","title":"Wasted in Jackson"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" "Not the Drinking" was added to BBC Radio Two A-List in October 2010 and remained there for two weeks.","title":"Wasted in Jackson"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" "Wasted In Jackson" entered the UK Album Chart at 84 on 31 October.","title":"Wasted in Jackson"},{"sentence_id":9,"text":" A fourth single, "Stuck", was released on 14 February 2011.","title":"Wasted in Jackson"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Young Hercules is a prequel series from the television series "".","title":"Young Hercules"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was aired on Fox Kids Network from September 12, 1998 to May 12, 1999.","title":"Young Hercules"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It lasted 1 season with 50 episodes and starred Ryan Gosling in the title role.","title":"Young Hercules"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The series was based on the Greek mythology hero, Hercules.","title":"Young Hercules"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Gigantic
